Node-assertable surface — the honest walk-gated verdict
-------------------------------------------------------
Nothing in this diff is node-assertable, and this is stated plainly (never fabricated):

  - The change is pure CSS in app.css. The Vitest suite renders component MARKUP
    (JSDOM / react-dom static markup) and asserts on class names, element counts,
    and rendered text — it does NOT load app.css or read computed styles. There is
    no CSS-property assertion surface in the suite to add to. (grep confirmed: no
    getComputedStyle / accent-color / ::file-selector-button read in src or tests.)
  - The design (brainstorm.md v4 FROZEN, Test plan sketch) predicts exactly this:
    "Zero new node tests (CSS-only; the base rule is walk-gated). Churned pins
    expected zero." The base rule, radio/checkbox accent, file-selector face, and
    color-scheme are all computed-style effects invisible to a markup assertion.
  - Therefore no new node test is added. The visual result (every control in the
    quiet-mono base look, radios/checkboxes with accent marks, native popups
    tracking color-scheme, the re-dressed tier/view toggles, the frameless carve-
    outs) is verified by the manual both-media walk, recorded below as a checklist.

