Specificity re-score (the :where() closure + exceptions winning)
----------------------------------------------------------------
  - Base arms all (0,0,1): `button`, `select`, and
    `input:where(:not([type="radio"]):not([type="checkbox"]))` — :where() zeroes the
    :not() pseudo-class weight, so the input arm is (0,0,1) not (0,2,1). Confirmed the
    class exceptions all outrank:
      .link-inspector-close   (0,1,0) > base — frameless border:none wins.
      .stage-node-remove      (0,1,0) > base — frameless border:none wins.
      .stage-node-rename      (0,1,0) > base — new border:none/background:transparent
                              strips the base box; input reads as an inline edit.
      .theme-toggle           (0,1,0) > base — own full dress wins.
      .app-header input[type="file"] (0,2,1) > base — outranks comfortably.
      .react-flow__controls-button   (0,1,0) > base — RF chrome wins; base only
                              contributes inert font/radius (accepted, per design).
  - Accepted leaks (stated in design, matching the RF note): the base's inert props
    (border-radius:0 / padding / font-family / font-size) leak onto the frameless
    exceptions where those exceptions don't set them. This does not un-frame anything
    (border/background are overridden) and is accepted for uniformity.

Both-media walk checklist (manual — vellum + cyanotype)
-------------------------------------------------------
This is the gate the node suite cannot express; run per the design's Test plan sketch:
  [ ] Every control app-wide (header upload + toggle, settings Recipe/Machines/clock/
      overrides, plans bar, chain builders, inspector mode/trip/fuel/derate, alt-
      compare + train buttons) reads medium-correct: mono face, --fg-muted ink,
      transparent ground, --border-soft hairline, square corners.
  [ ] The stage-node rename input, when editing a plate name, is UN-BOXED — no soft
      border, transparent ground, inline in the name bar (NOT a control box).
  [ ] Radios + checkboxes (inspector mode radios + the two derate/option checkboxes)
      show the --accent tint on their marks in BOTH media — native, never boxed.
  [ ] Native select popups + number spinners + the file picker track the medium via
      color-scheme (light on vellum, dark on cyanotype).
  [ ] File inputs: the button face (::file-selector-button) wears the base look;
      native-unstyled fallback acceptable where the pseudo is unsupported.
  [ ] Tier toggles re-dressed by the base (mono/muted/soft border), pointer intact;
      the active .tier-on button still shows the --accent fill + on-accent text.
  [ ] View toggle re-dressed by the base (mono/muted/soft border), 13px + its padding
      kept, pointer intact — its former ink border / panel ground / 4px radius gone.
  [ ] The frameless close ✕ (.link-inspector-close) and node remove ✕
      (.stage-node-remove) stay frameless (border:none), pointer intact.
  [ ] Contrast unchanged (audited tokens); no hardcoded-looking control chrome.
